# XKnot federation configuration template. Generated by packages/knot-config/src/schema.mjs.
#
# This file is not part of deployment. It only holds what the hub (xknot.si) issued:
# instance id, hub origin, issue date, and delegated-mailing credentials. Key names and semantics
# are the federation contract, see xknot.si/docs/FEDERATION.md §7.4; filename and location are this implementation's convention.
# Written by join-xknot.sh, mode 600.
#
#   ./ops/scripts/join-xknot.sh --payload ~/xknot-access.env
#   ./ops/scripts/join-xknot.sh --status
#
# Do not hand-fill it, and do not merge it into site.env or platform.env:
# the deploy script only reads those two, and joining doesn't need re-signing when switching machines for redeploy.
# An instance that doesn't join the federation doesn't need this file.
#
# Below, everything except the hub origin is left empty — no join payload, no federation.

# ---- XKnot federation ----
# The instance id in the hub roster (lowercase letters, digits, hyphens). Written into /api/health's instance, for the hub to verify identity.
# Example: wang
# XKNOT_INSTANCE_ID=
# The hub origin this instance joins. The delegated-mailing address derives from it.
# Example: https://xknot.si
XKNOT_HUB_ORIGIN=https://xknot.si
# The full delegated-mailing address. Empty derives from XKNOT_HUB_ORIGIN; only hand-written when switching entries.
# Example: https://xknot.si/api/federation/mail
# XKNOT_HUB_RELAY_URL=
# The delegated-mailing credential issued by the hub. Exists only in xknot.env; never enters mail, the repo, or the release package.
# XKNOT_HUB_RELAY_TOKEN=
# The public address issued by the hub. Part of the issued zone, consistent with the roster's url; the node only reads it.
# Example: https://wang.xknot.si
# XKNOT_ISSUED_URL=
# The issue date (YYYY-MM-DD). Part of the issued zone, reported outward as since.
# Example: 2026-10-20
# XKNOT_ISSUED_AT=
# The tier issued by the hub: free or paid (early demo / partner / community still readable). Part of the issued zone; empty means not reported outward.
# XKNOT_TIER=
# The status issued by the hub. Part of the issued zone; empty means not reported outward.
# XKNOT_STATUS=

